  "body": "## What changed\nThe 3D Pocket ladder names the tool diameter and stock allowance when erosion removes all open area.\nThe filled-model refusal keeps its existing text.\n\n## Cause\nThe ladder discarded the reason a level had no cutter-centre area.\nBoth cases reached the same final refusal.\n\n## Tests\n- `filled_pocket_names_the_model` pins the existing refusal for both entry points.\n- `narrow_pocket_names_the_tool` pins the narrow-area refusal for both entry points.\n- `stock_allowance_names_the_clearance_needed` pins nonzero stock allowance for both entry points.\n- Both new diagnostic pins failed before the fix.\n- Restoring the upstream ladder made both diagnostic pins fail again.\n- Restoring the fix made all three pins pass.\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings` passed.\n\n## Goldens moved\nNone.\nThe `.nc` and `.cl` diff stat is empty.\n\n## Not exercised\nThe STEP sample from #1706 was imported by `the_sample_as_imported_refuses_the_3d_pocket_by_name` and passed with the tool-clearance refusal.\nThe full `shared_face_bodies` suite passed (5 passed, 1 heavy test ignored).\nThe release gate was not run.\n\n## Overlaps\nNone found in open PRs for the three changed files.\n\nEffort: medium\n\nChangelog: 3D Pocket names tool clearance when the open area is too narrow to cut.\n\nFixes #1709\n",
